{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNUZwGUFBFj3ry58nbYn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012cC8a79xWuF5WGJBM836Ht","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /work/internal/roles/reviewers/security-review\ncat > Dockerfile <<'E'\n# Pinned tool image for the security-review aid (docs/proposal.md, Reviewer\n# loop, step 3). Tools: gosec, gitleaks and semgrep, plus jq.\n#\n# Verification pending human: this file was written without network access.\n#   - The versions below were not rebuilt from this file. Build it, run the\n#     integration test (`go test -tags integration ./internal/roles -run\n#     SecurityReviewAid`) and confirm the versions are current before merge.\n#   - gosec and gitleaks are built from source with the image's Go (integrity\n#     from the Go module proxy and checksum database, as golangci-lint is in the\n#     lint scanner's image). Replace the versions by the ones the owner approves.\n#   - semgrep is installed from PyPI at a pinned version. Add --require-hashes\n#     with a hash-pinned requirements file once the hashes are verified.\n#   - jq's checksums are the ones in scanners/lint/Dockerfile.\n#\n# The image does NOT copy `aid`, `normalize.jq` or `rules/`: the executor\n# mounts this role directory read-only, so the mounted files are the ones that\n# run. The aid runs under --network none, so semgrep never fetches rules.\n\nARG GO_IMAGE=golang:1.27.4-trixie@sha256:f18c3d73a184fb0582828510722e723b63a93f7188d11dd223d9be6f6880e65d\n\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE} AS gotools\nARG GOSEC_VERSION=v2.22.0\nARG GITLEAKS_VERSION=v8.30.0\nRUN CGO_ENABLED=0 GOBIN=/out go install github.com/securego/gosec/v2/cmd/gosec@${GOSEC_VERSION} \\\n && CGO_ENABLED=0 GOBIN=/out go install github.com/zricethezav/gitleaks/v8@${GITLEAKS_VERSION}\n\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE} AS tools\nARG TARGETARCH\nARG JQ_VERSION=1.8.2\nARG JQ_SHA256_AMD64=b1c22172dd303f3be49e935aa56aa48a8b7a46e0bc838b4997d3bb451495870f\nARG JQ_SHA256_ARM64=8b85c817833814ddca00a144c33705546355afccf0cf39b188f3cdb48b852309\nRUN set -eu; \\\n    case \"${TARGETARCH}\" in \\\n      amd64) jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_AMD64}\" ;; \\\n      arm64) jq_sha=\"${JQ_SHA256_ARM64}\" ;; \\\n      *) echo \"unsupported arch: ${TARGETARCH}\" >&2; exit 1 ;; \\\n    esac; \\\n    mkdir /out; \\\n    curl -fsSL -o /out/jq \"https://github.com/jqlang/jq/releases/download/jq-${JQ_VERSION}/jq-linux-${TARGETARCH}\"; \\\n    echo \"${jq_sha}  /out/jq\" | sha256sum -c -; \\\n    chmod 0755 /out/jq\n\nFROM ${GO_IMAGE}\nARG SEMGREP_VERSION=1.140.0\nRUN apt-get update \\\n && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends python3 python3-venv \\\n && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/* \\\n && python3 -m venv /opt/semgrep \\\n && /opt/semgrep/bin/pip install --no-cache-dir \"semgrep==${SEMGREP_VERSION}\" \\\n && ln -s /opt/semgrep/bin/semgrep /usr/local/bin/semgrep\nCOPY --from=gotools /out/gosec /usr/local/bin/gosec\nCOPY --from=gotools /out/gitleaks /usr/local/bin/gitleaks\nCOPY --from=tools /out/jq /usr/local/bin/jq\n# The executor's /tmp is a noexec tmpfs: TMPDIR lives in /var/tmp. GOTOOLCHAIN=local:\n# no implicit toolchain switching. SEMGREP_* keep semgrep offline and out of $HOME.\nENV GOTOOLCHAIN=local \\\n    TMPDIR=/var/tmp \\\n    SEMGREP_SEND_METRICS=off \\\n    SEMGREP_ENABLE_VERSION_CHECK=0\nE\npython3 - <<'E'\np='prompt.txt'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef sub(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s,a\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\nsub('''- .ard-input/N/issue.md (the issue as filed)''','''- .ard-input/N/aid.jsonl, when it exists: the results of pinned tools\n  that ard ran before you (see \"Checks\"). One JSON object per line with\n  tool, rule, file, line, severity and message, after a banner and a line\n  that counts what was kept and dropped. A banner that says the aid\n  failed replaces the results.\n- .ard-input/N/issue.md (the issue as filed)''')\nsub('''Deterministic tools find; you explain, rank and confirm. Run each tool''','''Deterministic tools find; you explain, rank and confirm.\n\nWhen .ard-input/N/aid.jsonl exists, read it first. ard already ran\ngitleaks, gosec and semgrep (with a vendored rule set) over the changed\nfiles, so do not run them again. Treat each line as a lead: confirm it in\nthe code, drop it as a false positive, or rank it. A result carries no\nmatched text; never ask a tool to print it. Say in ## Checks how many\nresults you confirmed and how many you dropped. A secret that gitleaks\nfound on an added line is added to your review by ard whether or not you\nlist it, and the verdict is then changes; still describe it. If the file\nsays the aid failed, say so in ## Checks, run the tools below yourself as\nfar as you can, and know that ard will not let this review approve. Still\ndo the Dependencies check below and your own reading.\n\nWhen aid.jsonl is absent, run the tools yourself. Run each tool''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -n \"run when installed\" -i prompt.txt"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":718,"cache_read_input_tokens":85205,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":718},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53a4b6cd-1947-4c9b-876e-e420c4c51cec","uuid":"a2b7c038-b591-4b38-9594-5a36f7e49fe9","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:38:35.066Z","request_id":"req_011ChNUZvveA6NFwwniqFWUb"}
