{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNVCkjzBGX39nMfaiju6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L9REjWAjLh6qSknA75hkgw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='docs/proposal.md'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef sub(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert a in s,a\n    s=s.replace(a,b,1)\naid=('3. **Run the aid, then the agent.** After the pin, a role with an executable `aid` in its directory (reviewers only, like a scanner\\'s `scan`; #205) has it run by the controller as its own executor job at the pinned head, before the agent, so the findings of its deterministic tools do not depend on the host or on the agent choosing to run them. The tool finds; the agent explains, ranks and confirms. The aid job is read-only, has no `Env` and no `Fixed` entries (no model credential, no GitHub token), runs with `--network none` under Docker (a role `Dockerfile` or `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`; known CVEs stay with the `cve` scanner, so the aid never queries vulnerability databases), and has its own timeout of 5 minutes (shorter if the role\\'s is), counted inside the review job\\'s timeout: the agent gets what is left, at least one minute. Its inputs are `.ard-input/<issue#>/changed.txt` (one path per line, `.ard/<issue#>/` left out) and `diff.patch`. Its output is JSONL on stdout, one object per result with exactly `tool`, `rule`, `file`, `line`, `severity` (`critical`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `info`) and `message`, capped at 256 KiB (more is a failure). ard validates it: a line that is not JSON, has an unknown key, a bad tool, rule, severity or line, or a path that is absolute, has `..` or is not in `changed.txt` is dropped and counted; a message is redacted, cut at 1 KiB and secret-scanned like a log, and a line that still trips the scanner is dropped. Matched text is never kept: the aid must print rule ids and positions only. The result is written to `.ard-input/<issue#>/aid.jsonl` and is the first of the agent\\'s untrusted inputs; the starter prompt reads it first and runs the tools itself only when the file is absent. **Failure:** a failed, timed-out or invalid aid (any dropped line counts as invalid) never stops the review. The input says the aid failed and why, and close-out turns an `approve` into `changes` with a note. **Blocking:** a `gitleaks` result on a line the PR added becomes a blocking `high` finding with a `[secret]` message that ard adds to the review in code (carrying the rule id only); the agent cannot drop it, and an `approve` becomes `changes`. gosec and semgrep results stay advisory. Both rules apply only to roles that have an `aid`. **Host mode:** with no role `Dockerfile` and no `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`, the aid runs on the host, as ard-owned code that reads but never executes PR code; its environment holds no credential, but nothing enforces its network, and it runs as the controller\\'s uid without a sandbox: the residual risk of #84 applies to it too. The starter `security-review/aid` pins gosec, gitleaks and semgrep (vendored local rules, `--metrics=off`, `--disable-nosem`) in the role\\'s `Dockerfile`, built on the default ard-agent image (k8s role images stay with #245). 4. **Run the agent** with')\nsub('3. **Run the agent** with',aid.replace('4. **Run the agent** with','Then **run the agent** with'))\nsub(' Running pinned tools in controller code is #205.',' The role\\'s `aid` (#205) runs gitleaks, gosec and semgrep in controller code before the agent (Reviewer loop, step 3); the prompt reads `aid.jsonl` first and runs the tools itself only when it is absent. It ships a `Dockerfile` (the default ard-agent image plus the pinned tools), so it runs under Docker.')\nsub('No Dockerfile: host mode with the #84 warning until #55. ','')\nsub('gitleaks, gosec, semgrep with local rules (run by the agent when installed; controller-run aids are #205)','gitleaks, gosec, semgrep with local rules (run by the role\\'s `aid` before the agent; the agent runs them only without `aid.jsonl`)')\nsub('├── reviewers/<name>/    # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts','├── reviewers/<name>/    # prompt.txt; optional Dockerfile, scripts, aid (executable)')\nsub('and `scan` is written `100755`','and `scan` and `aid` are written `100755`')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\ngrep -c \"#205\" docs/proposal.md; grep -rn \"docscheck\" -l internal | head -2; sed -i '' '/^- #205 Reviewer aid step/d' docs/TODO.md; git diff --stat docs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":148512,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2303},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53a4b6cd-1947-4c9b-876e-e420c4c51cec","uuid":"a4eb30cb-5039-4ac3-8618-47a022337fe4","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:46:52.031Z","request_id":"req_011ChNVCk1LorpyqwyX9d7Yw"}
