{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChNVLmVcZjMhudM5M3pYw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I implemented the `aid` step for issue #205 and wrote the report to `.ard/205/worker-engineer.md`. `go test ./...` and `make lint` pass. The Docker integration test and the real tools were not run, so the starter aid script and Dockerfile are untested end to end.\n\n**What it does**\n- **Run:** A reviewer role with an `aid` script now has the controller run it before the agent, in its own job. The job is read-only, has no credentials, uses no network under Docker, and gets 5 minutes, counted inside the review's timeout.\n- **Validation:** The aid's output is validated before the agent sees it. Bad lines are dropped and counted, and messages are redacted and secret-scanned.\n- **Agent input:** The result goes to the agent as `aid.jsonl`, or as a note saying the aid failed and why.\n- **Blocking and failure rules:** Close-out applies your decisions. A gitleaks hit on an added line becomes a blocking `high` finding that the agent cannot drop. A failed, timed-out or invalid aid can only return `changes`. Both apply only to roles that have an `aid`.\n- **Config:** Config discovery, `ard config check` and `ard init` handle the new script (init writes it `100755`).\n- **Starter role:** The security-review role gets an `aid` script, `normalize.jq`, vendored semgrep rules, a `Dockerfile` on the ard-agent image, and a prompt that reads `aid.jsonl` first.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md` is updated, and I removed the #205 line from `docs/TODO.md`.\n\n**Needs a human before merge**\n- **Dockerfile pins:** I wrote it without network access. The gosec, gitleaks and semgrep versions are unverified guesses with no checksums. Build the image and run `TestIntegrationSecurityReviewAid`, which also needs Docker and `ARD_AGENT_IMAGE`, before merge.\n- **Fixtures:** The #43 S1, S4 and S5 fixtures aren't in the repo, so the integration test builds stand-in fixtures: shell injection, a runtime-built secret and disabled TLS verification.\n- **Dogfooding config:** Copying the starter aid into this repository's own `.ard/reviewers/` is a protected-path change that I left to you.\n\n**Test changes**\n- **Security-review role test:** It no longer expects the role to be host-untrusted, because it now has a `Dockerfile`.\n- **Prompt cap:** I trimmed the prompt to stay under the existing 16 KiB limit.\n- **gofmt message:** `make lint` prints one gofmt message about `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`. It is an existing, deliberately broken fixture that I didn't touch.\n\nThe untracked `.ard-input/205/` files are the controller's inputs, not part of the change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_read_input_tokens":156233,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1555},"output_tokens":750,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"53a4b6cd-1947-4c9b-876e-e420c4c51cec","uuid":"42be5faa-b8fe-40f8-bc7b-abdecfd109e6","timestamp":"2026-11-24T21:48:34.828Z","request_id":"req_011ChNVLmMgB9ejiZJ9SogXS"}
